course: dictionary
lesson: 2056
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Consciousness is one of these words. «A person in space without a suit would not explode; they would lose consciousness in about 15 seconds» means they would stop being awake and aware of what is around them.
explain: The clue is «lose», and the next part of the sentence, «need rescue within a minute or two». Someone who loses consciousness faints or is knocked out, so they cannot notice what is happening. Always ask: what does this word mean in this sentence? Then try your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Consciousness can also mean caring about something, as in «environmental consciousness», or it can mean your mind, your thoughts and feelings, as in «the idea entered her consciousness». Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Consciousness means being awake and aware of what is around you.
fact: Lose consciousness means faint or be knocked out, so you are not awake or aware.
fact: Regain consciousness means become awake and aware again.
fact: Environmental consciousness means caring about the environment and being aware of problems with it.
fact: Consciousness can also mean your mind, your thoughts and feelings.
exercise: «She lost consciousness after she hit her head on the ice.» What does lost consciousness mean? | She got a new coat | She won a race on the ice | She was very cold and wet | *She fainted and was no longer awake
exercise: «Our class shows real environmental consciousness by picking up litter every week.» What does environmental consciousness mean? | *Caring about the environment and being aware of it | Knowing how to swim in a pond | A test about the weather | Being very tired after a long walk
exercise: «The idea slowly entered her consciousness.» Which meaning fits here? | Her shoes, which were new | *Her mind, her thoughts and feelings | Her garden, which was large | Her ears, so she could hear it
test: «He regained consciousness in the ambulance.» What does regained consciousness mean? | *He became awake and aware again | He fell asleep for a week | He was too busy to speak | He was given a new bike
test: «Our school has a strong environmental consciousness.» Which meaning fits best? | A special kind of cake | Being awake in the middle of the night | *Caring about and being aware of the environment | A loud noise in the hall
exam: «If someone loses consciousness, what should you do first?» | Give them a big drink of water straight away | Tell them to get up and walk | *Call for help and check their breathing | Leave them alone and go home
